# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Some tokens (e.g. USDC) may DOS in `SlashingHandler.sol#handleSlashing()` when trying to send to address (0).

## Proof of Concept
The `SlashingHandler.sol#handleSlashing()` function is used in the `Vault.sol#slashAssets()` function to slash a certain amount of assets in the vault with the slashing handler contract.
```solidity
    function slashAssets(uint256 totalAssetsToSlash, address slashingHandler)
        external
        onlyCore
        returns (uint256 transferAmount)
    {
        transferAmount = Math.min(totalAssets(), totalAssetsToSlash);

        // Approve to the handler and then call the handler which will draw the funds
        SafeTransferLib.safeApproveWithRetry(asset(), slashingHandler, transferAmount);
202:    ISlashingHandler(slashingHandler).handleSlashing(IERC20(asset()), transferAmount);

        emit Slashed(transferAmount);
    }
```
In the `SlashingHandler.sol#handleSlashing()` function, the `SlashingHandler` contrant pulls the assets form the vault and send them to address(0).
```solidity
    function handleSlashing(IERC20 token, uint256 amount) external {
        if (amount == 0) revert ZeroAmount();
        if (!_config().supportedAssets[token]) revert UnsupportedAsset();

        SafeTransferLib.safeTransferFrom(address(token), msg.sender, address(this), amount);
        // Below is where custom logic for each asset lives
58:     SafeTransferLib.safeTransfer(address(token), address(0), amount);
    }
```
However, some tokens (e.g. USDC) may DOS in `SlashingHandler.sol#handleSlashing()` when trying to send to address (0).
https://etherscan.io/address/0x43506849d7c04f9138d1a2050bbf3a0c054402dd#code
```solidity
    function _transfer(
        address from,
        address to,
        uint256 value
    ) internal override {
-->     require(from != address(0), "ERC20: transfer from the zero address");
-->     require(to != address(0), "ERC20: transfer to the zero address");
        require(
            value <= _balanceOf(from),
            "ERC20: transfer amount exceeds balance"
        );

        _setBalance(from, _balanceOf(from).sub(value));
        _setBalance(to, _balanceOf(to).add(value));
        emit Transfer(from, to, value);
    }
```
Therefor, the `SlashingHandler.sol#handleSlashing()` may DOS when trying to send to address (0) and the core function of the protocol may be damaged.

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Instead of sending assets to address(0), use a burn mechanism.


