# Vulnerability details

When registering a Dss the Dss can either choose to slash or not slash, if the Dss chooses not to slash they set the `maxSlashablePercentageWad` to 1 which indicates no slashing as zero is the default meaning not registered.

The issue arises because setting `maxSlashablePercentageWad` to 1 (indicating no slashing) is effectively a `0.000000000000000001%` slashing rate, which is still non-zero and thus allows for slashing, albeit minimal.
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-karak/blob/main/src%2FCore.sol#L262-L263
```solidity
